<item><title>Benin plans a learning city in each of its six development hubs</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-plans-a-learning-city-in-each-of-its-six-development-71f8c9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-plans-a-learning-city-in-each-of-its-six-development-71f8c9/</guid><category>Benin</category><description>Decentralisation Minister Janvier Yahouédéhou presented the plan in Cotonou and cited Porto-Novo, admitted to UNESCO&apos;s learning-cities network in 2025, as the model.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:51:48 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" length="29969" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Wadagni secures initial agreement for eight-country UEMOA summit in 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/wadagni-secures-initial-agreement-for-eight-country-uemoa-f3b0b1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/wadagni-secures-initial-agreement-for-eight-country-uemoa-f3b0b1/</guid><category>Benin</category><description>The Beninese president consulted leaders from Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger after months of deadlock over holding a top-level meeting.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:18:34 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" length="29969" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Japan funds Benin malaria pilot with two spray drones</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/japan-funds-benin-malaria-pilot-with-two-spray-drones-2a8123/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/japan-funds-benin-malaria-pilot-with-two-spray-drones-2a8123/</guid><category>Benin</category><description>The $2.3 million programme also supplies 12 backpack sprayers for mosquito-control work in 10 districts through February 2027.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:17:45 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" length="29969" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Benin, Senegal and Djibouti set plans for out-of-school youth training</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-senegal-and-djibouti-set-plans-for-out-of-school-04c7f8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-senegal-and-djibouti-set-plans-for-out-of-school-04c7f8/</guid><category>Benin</category><description>A Cotonou meeting reviewed the three-country training scheme and outlined national rollout plans, trainer preparation and field monitoring.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:13:58 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" length="29969" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Benin proposes CFA174,826 billion for health in 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-proposes-cfa174-826-billion-for-health-in-2027-3b488d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-proposes-cfa174-826-billion-for-health-in-2027-3b488d/</guid><category>Benin</category><description>Health Minister Benjamin Ignace Bodounrin Hounkpatin told lawmakers the funds would support urgent care, new hospitals and existing facilities.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:03:04 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-proposes-cfa174-826-billion-for-health-in-2027-3b488d/share.jpg" length="40372" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bj/benin-proposes-cfa174-826-billion-for-health-in-2027-3b488d/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
